	(text "Project References:\nhttps://digilent.com/reference/programmable-logic/arty-a7/reference-manual\nhttps://digilent.com/reference/_media/programmable-logic/arty-a7/arty-a7-e2-sch.pdf\nhttps://github.com/snhobbs/scopefun-hardware/tree/master/KiCadSource\nhttps://github.com/arm8686/FT2232HL-Board/blob/master/FT2232HL%20Board%20sch%20V3.6.pdf\n\nAMD Documentation:\nhttps://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/ug470_7Series_Config\nhttps://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/ds181_Artix_7_Data_Sheet\nhttps://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/wp484-a7-s7-ddr2-3-pcb\nhttps://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug908-vivado-programming-debugging/JTAG-Cables-and-Devices-Supported-by-hw_server\nhttps://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug586_7Series_MIS/Trace-Lengths\n\nProject Goals:\nRun ML/MPC/LQR on an FPGA\nUse DDR3 to load weights/matrices from an SD card\n\nStackup:\nL1: Signal & Placement\nL2: Ground\nL3: DDR3L\nL4: Ground\nL5: DDR3L\nL6: Ground\nL7: Power\nL8: Signal & Placement\n\nDDR Routing:\nAccording to WP484, route single ended as 50ohm, diff as 100ohm\nChose closest ODT to 50ohm"
